requirements.detail:
Requires the material of gauges to be of suitable quality gauge steel capable of retaining dimensions during ageing and heat treatment while remaining wear resistant [3]. Standard steel designations recommended from IS 3748 : 1990 include: 
a) XT 215 Cr 12 for plain plug gauges; 
b) T 105 Cr 5 Mn 2 for ring gauges; 
b) T 105 Cr 5 (typographically printed as T1OSCr5) for thread plug gauges; 
c) T 90 V 2 (typographically printed as T9OV2) for thread ring gauges [3, 4].

Gauges must be legibly marked or tagged (using an aluminium plate for miniature plug gauges) indicating: 
a) Nominal size (per IS 14365); 
b) Class of tolerance with type of deviation and amount of tolerance (plain gauges) or tolerance class (thread gauges only - check plug gauges append 'Tcp' after tolerance class); 
c) The word 'GO' and 'NOT GO' on respective gauges; 
d) Manufacturer's name or trade mark; 
e) Red paint on 'NOT GO' gauges; 
f) 'Check' or 'Wear Check' marked on check plug and wear check plug gauges respectively [4].
